      "fingerprint": "536a5346a6d8846d191bd39c9a8b2ad87c482cc5da53ee4ebda257d8507ee507",
      "kind": "editorial",
      "status": "blocked",
      "issues": [
        "- The claim that the adjective/pronoun test works for possessive \"my/your/his\" is incorrect: \"my\" and \"your\" cannot stand alone as pronouns (only \"his\" can); the possessive pronouns are \"mine, yours, his, hers, ours, theirs\" → The test works for demonstrative and interrogative, but for possessive the pronoun forms differ from the adjective forms."
      ],
